{title: Scales Fall Down}
{subtitle: Acts 9:1–19}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 69}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Something like scales fell from his eyes
He got up and was baptized
The hunter of the church became the Lord's chosen instrument
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Every man and every woman who belongs to the Way
He will drag them back in chains to Jerusalem that day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Suddenly a light from [B]heaven flashed around him
He fell [C#]to the ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Saul, Saul, why [G#m]are you persecuting [D#m]me
Who are [D#m]you, Lord
I am Je[F#]sus, whom you [C#]are perse[F#]cuting
Get [G#]up and go into the [D#m]city [F#6]
Light [D#m]on the Damascus road
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Three [F#]days in [C#]the darkness, and he would not eat [F#]or [G#]drink
Eyes wide open seeing [D#m]nothing, nothing left to do but think
In a house on Straight Street there the blinded man would pray
While the Lord called Ananias and sent him on his way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Suddenly a light from heaven flashed around him
He fell to the ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me
Who are you, Lord
[B]I am Jesus, whom you are per[C#]secuting
Get up and [G#]go into the city
[D#m]Light on the [D#m]Damascus road
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Broth[F#]er Saul, the [C#]Lord Jesus
[F#]Has sent me [G#]so that you may see a[D#m]gain
Something [D#m]like scales fell from his eyes
He [F#]got up [C#]and was baptized
The hunter of [F#]the [G#]church became the Lord's chosen [D#m]instrument
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Light on the Damascus road
Scales fall down and he can see
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
